From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jokubas Maciulaitis <ubitas52@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:29:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: ubi: write the fastmap when converting at attach

With fm_autoconvert, an image without a fastmap gets one only on the
next volume change, when a fastmap pool runs out, or at detach. A
device that mounts its root file system from UBI read-only, keeps
little else there and is switched off rather than shut down can go on
attaching by scanning at every boot, here 1.9 s for a 64 MiB NAND.
Write the fastmap right after attaching by scanning instead.
---
 drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
index fb121b6..b36f0f8 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
@@ -1058,6 +1058,20 @@ int ubi_attach_mtd_dev(struct mtd_info *mtd, int ubi_num,
 	wake_up_process(ubi->bgt_thread);
 	spin_unlock(&ubi->wl_lock);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MTD_UBI_FASTMAP
+	/*
+	 * Attached by scanning with fm_autoconvert set: write the fastmap
+	 * now. Otherwise it waits for a volume change, a pool running out or
+	 * a detach, which a device that only reads its root file system and
+	 * is switched off may never see.
+	 */
+	if (!ubi->fm && !ubi->fm_disabled) {
+		err = ubi_update_fastmap(ubi);
+		if (err)
+			ubi_msg(ubi, "Unable to write a new fastmap: %i", err);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	ubi_devices[ubi_num] = ubi;
 	ubi_notify_all(ubi, UBI_VOLUME_ADDED, NULL);
 	return ubi_num;
